# TEMPLATE for scripts/mirror-private-terms.txt — the EXTRA site terms that
# scripts/mirror-snapshot.sh must never find in the published snapshot.
#
# Copy to scripts/mirror-private-terms.txt (gitignored) and put your own terms there. The
# real file is optional: without it the sanitizer still scrubs and checks everything it can
# derive from cluster.env (node aliases, management IPs and their /24, the fabric /16, the
# link-local range, the login name, *.ts.net names) — this file is for the terms that
# appear NOWHERE in cluster.env and therefore cannot be derived.
#
# Format: one extended-regex per line, matched CASE-INSENSITIVELY against every text file
# of the snapshot. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. These terms are
# NOT rewritten, only checked: a single occurrence fails the scan, so that the fix happens
# in the source file rather than being silently papered over. The terms themselves are
# never printed by the report — a hit is shown as `path:line` plus a masked excerpt.
#
# The dummy entries below are the CATEGORIES worth listing, with example values; replace
# them, and delete the ones that do not apply.

# The COMMON STEM of the node aliases, when they share one. The per-rank rewrite only knows
# the exact aliases of NODES, so a generic form written in prose (`nodeN`, `node<N>`,
# `node*`) survives it; listing the stem here is what catches those.
gx10-

# The workstation's own host name (it shows up in shell prompts, paths and pasted output)
my-workstation

# The tailnet / MagicDNS name, on its own as well as inside a *.ts.net name
example-tailnet

# City, site or rack name used in notes and bench write-ups
springfield

# Any second login name that is not the one in RELAY_DEST
bob

# A personal domain quoted in e-mail addresses or URLs
example-domain\.test
